WEBVTT

00:47.631 --> 00:48.632
Hello?

00:51.468 --> 00:54.721
I… I can… I can barely hear you.

00:56.682 --> 00:57.683
What?

01:00.102 --> 01:01.103
Where?

01:02.187 --> 01:04.815
I've been asleep for a day?

01:44.021 --> 01:49.401
The entry mentioned a plague,
which Gerrie connected to 1702.

01:50.402 --> 01:51.612
And with that,

01:52.237 --> 01:56.450
we are able to deduce that the journal
belonged to Sarah Westcott Warren.

01:56.533 --> 01:57.659
And…

01:58.660 --> 01:59.870
Here.

02:14.718 --> 02:15.719
Thank you.

02:16.720 --> 02:21.642
We thought maybe the cursed item might
be buried with Richard Warren.

02:22.809 --> 02:25.687
So Wyck suggested we dig him up.

02:26.563 --> 02:28.148
And so, we did just that.

02:30.567 --> 02:32.194
You did what?

02:33.362 --> 02:34.988
We dug up Richard Warren's coffin.

02:38.408 --> 02:40.410
You dug up the founder's corpse?

02:40.494 --> 02:42.246
- Yeah, it's over there.
- Yeah, it's here.

02:55.259 --> 02:56.593
Are you out of your fucking minds?

02:56.677 --> 02:58.512
All right, just listen
to what she's telling you.

02:58.595 --> 03:00.681
- Oh, my God. He's in there?
- No. He's upstairs.

03:00.764 --> 03:01.849
We moved him.

03:04.601 --> 03:05.853
Why…

03:05.936 --> 03:07.813
Why did you move him?

03:07.896 --> 03:09.189
Because he's still alive.

03:11.149 --> 03:12.484
What?

03:12.568 --> 03:16.780
But we have been able
to communicate a little through notes.

03:19.950 --> 03:20.951
What?

03:21.034 --> 03:24.538
Richard Warren is in that room.

03:24.621 --> 03:25.664
He's waiting for you.

03:26.540 --> 03:28.458
What do you me…

03:28.542 --> 03:30.085
Why would he be waiting for me?

03:30.169 --> 03:33.463
He will only communicate with the "Lord
Island Protector." We assume that's you.

03:33.547 --> 03:35.924
Yeah, look at this. See this?

03:36.008 --> 03:37.009
Huh?

03:39.011 --> 03:40.554
Yeah. Yeah.

03:42.806 --> 03:43.974
You go in there

03:44.892 --> 03:46.935
and get him to tell you

03:47.561 --> 03:49.521
how the fuck to open this thing.

03:51.732 --> 03:53.275
- No!
- No, no, no! No!

03:53.942 --> 03:55.277
Don't…

03:55.360 --> 03:57.029
Don't try to do it yourself.

03:57.779 --> 03:58.989
Get him to do it.

03:59.698 --> 04:00.699
Here.

04:51.500 --> 04:53.210
I'll give you two your privacy.

06:47.574 --> 06:48.700
I forgot one thing.

06:58.335 --> 07:00.087
You can talk?

07:02.214 --> 07:03.215
Aye.

07:07.803 --> 07:09.054
How…

07:11.974 --> 07:13.684
How are you still alive?

07:16.228 --> 07:22.359
I was tricked by a devil
and betrayed by my lessers.

07:23.193 --> 07:26.363
But an evil power sustains me.

07:28.073 --> 07:30.534
What do you mean?
Is that… Is that what this is?

07:32.703 --> 07:33.745
Is it?

07:36.582 --> 07:39.501
Can… Can you open this?

07:47.968 --> 07:49.595
Loosen these.

07:53.098 --> 07:54.641
Sure, yeah. I mean…

07:54.725 --> 07:57.436
Well, I can… I can loosen them a bit.

08:12.492 --> 08:14.453
Yeah, let's…
Yeah, let's get those off you.

08:44.816 --> 08:45.901
What is this?

08:47.778 --> 08:51.031
I thought it was my salvation.

08:52.950 --> 08:56.537
We couldn't even find vermin
to sate our hunger.

08:57.788 --> 08:59.957
Some ate the corpses,

09:00.541 --> 09:03.001
others gorged on dirt.

09:03.794 --> 09:10.259
I was contemplating how to end my own life
with my own hand when I saw it.

09:15.764 --> 09:17.099
Sorry, forgot my purse.

09:25.858 --> 09:26.859
What…

09:28.819 --> 09:30.320
What was it you saw?

09:33.407 --> 09:36.159
A simple morsel of food.

09:37.369 --> 09:39.079
A mushroom.

09:40.664 --> 09:42.165
I thanked God.

09:43.542 --> 09:46.545
But something else came to me.

09:52.759 --> 09:54.178
What was it?

09:57.598 --> 09:58.599
A demon?

10:00.058 --> 10:01.852
The island itself?

10:03.478 --> 10:08.609
But I was starving,
and it was starving too.

10:09.943 --> 10:14.656
The covenant was offered
for my settlement's salvation,

10:14.740 --> 10:18.076
and I signed that pact

10:18.160 --> 10:23.373
with my own blood, feces and semen.

10:35.844 --> 10:38.055
What did you offer in return?

10:39.056 --> 10:41.391
If I had refused,

10:42.476 --> 10:44.478
none of you would be here.

10:45.729 --> 10:47.314
Maybe that would've been better.

10:48.190 --> 10:53.487
It's easy to judge when
your island is flourishing around you.

10:53.570 --> 10:54.655
Flourishing?

10:56.114 --> 11:00.244
My son is stuck on a fucking hell rock.

11:08.126 --> 11:10.546
I think it spoke to me.

11:15.425 --> 11:16.426
Did you follow it?

11:16.510 --> 11:17.511
No.

11:20.305 --> 11:21.974
What did it want?

11:23.475 --> 11:29.481
It knows frightened men
will do desperate things.

11:31.775 --> 11:33.068
What does that mean?

11:36.154 --> 11:39.157
I want to see my children's things.

12:07.477 --> 12:09.813
Every second in that coffin,

12:10.814 --> 12:12.774
I imagined their deaths.

12:56.235 --> 12:57.861
Sarah.

13:09.248 --> 13:10.249
So sad.

13:31.228 --> 13:33.146
As long as there are men with my blood,

13:33.897 --> 13:37.276
you are bound to the covenant.
But I am the last.

13:38.402 --> 13:39.778
What are you saying?

13:41.029 --> 13:42.447
Take me out to sea,

13:43.365 --> 13:47.661
past the point where sailors fear.

13:49.246 --> 13:50.998
Once I am beyond its grip,

13:52.499 --> 13:54.168
without the hex upon me,

13:55.335 --> 13:58.630
I believe I will age and die.

13:59.798 --> 14:01.717
With my bloodline gone,

14:02.217 --> 14:05.971
my death will free the island
from its curse.

14:08.223 --> 14:10.767
First of all,
we don't know that this will kill him.

14:10.851 --> 14:12.519
There's only one way to find out.

14:12.603 --> 14:15.898
Second of all,
the island's not gonna let him go easy.

14:15.981 --> 14:17.858
It's dangerous enough out there.

14:17.941 --> 14:21.528
At sea, at night,
let alone sailing with weak men.

14:21.612 --> 14:23.697
And no, I'm not talking about him.

14:23.780 --> 14:25.824
Anything can happen out there.

14:25.908 --> 14:29.745
The fact that you don't know that
tells me how dangerous this really is.

14:34.625 --> 14:35.626
Last night…

14:39.379 --> 14:40.631
I felt a presence.

14:40.714 --> 14:41.715
I did.

14:42.382 --> 14:44.801
I don't know what it is
and I don't know what it wants.

14:45.594 --> 14:47.179
I know we have to end it.

14:48.430 --> 14:50.015
I know we have to try.

14:57.272 --> 14:59.775
He's not on my boat
unless he's in the goddamn coffin.

15:05.489 --> 15:08.325
Wyck will take us out.

15:08.867 --> 15:12.579
But there will be people on the dock.

15:12.663 --> 15:18.961
So I have to ask, would you be willing
to get back inside the coffin?

15:19.545 --> 15:22.422
Just… Just until we're on the boat.

15:26.385 --> 15:28.345
- Just until we're on the boat.
- Yeah.

15:34.101 --> 15:35.102
Yeah. Okay.

15:36.395 --> 15:37.396
Tom.

15:46.113 --> 15:47.781
Oh, shit.

15:47.865 --> 15:49.116
What's he doing here?

15:50.075 --> 15:53.620
Someone may have reported my screaming.
Let me talk to him.

15:53.704 --> 15:55.247
What? Hold on. Hold on.

15:55.330 --> 15:56.331
Tom.

15:57.332 --> 15:58.333
I got this.

16:06.258 --> 16:09.511
Well, Patricia strikes again.

16:09.595 --> 16:12.472
Lost my keys, found my keys.
It was great to see…

16:12.556 --> 16:13.724
Have a good night.

16:13.807 --> 16:14.975
All right. You too.

16:15.058 --> 16:16.143
- Yeah.
- You…

16:27.237 --> 16:28.739
You should just go home.

16:33.744 --> 16:34.745
Patricia.

16:35.245 --> 16:37.206
Come here. Get out of my Jeep.

16:37.289 --> 16:39.374
What the hell are you doing?

16:39.458 --> 16:40.751
Patricia.

16:40.834 --> 16:41.960
Come here. Get…

16:44.129 --> 16:46.131
- I swear to God…
- Oh, my God.

16:47.674 --> 16:49.593
Patricia, what the hell are you doing?

16:49.676 --> 16:51.470
You better listen. Patricia!

16:52.554 --> 16:54.389
Stop this! Sto… Stop this!

16:54.890 --> 16:55.974
Come here!

16:56.558 --> 16:57.559
Let's go.

17:36.682 --> 17:41.520
Lot of fishermen learn the hard way
that you don't go too far from the island.

17:41.603 --> 17:45.524
It's like our own Bermuda Triangle
out there.

17:48.402 --> 17:52.739
So, we'll stop two minutes
before we get to this line.

17:54.575 --> 17:56.952
That's the dead zone.

17:57.035 --> 17:58.954
Crossing it will trigger this light.

18:00.747 --> 18:05.669
Beyond this buoy, people like me
don't tend to come back.

18:08.088 --> 18:11.842
Anyway, I'm gonna stop the boat
at the two-minute mark.

18:11.925 --> 18:16.263
You can put him on the dinghy from there
and take him the rest of the way yourself.

18:17.347 --> 18:20.392
Is two minutes cutting it too close
for you?

18:21.977 --> 18:24.646
You won't be able to row
on that thing much longer.

18:27.816 --> 18:32.154
Let's get him past the buoy and
send him to hell so we can end all this.

18:34.239 --> 18:36.617
The devil has hovered over this city,

18:37.117 --> 18:38.368
made it his own.

18:38.952 --> 18:40.996
The people in it are his.

18:41.496 --> 18:44.833
Evil has triumphed over good here.

18:45.709 --> 18:47.461
Look at my church.

18:47.544 --> 18:49.171
I have no parish…

18:49.963 --> 18:52.716
I have… I have weed. If you… If you want.

18:52.799 --> 18:55.552
We just have to smoke it outside.

18:56.970 --> 18:59.056
Your dad isn't coming home soon, is he?

18:59.139 --> 19:00.766
No, no, no. Not for a while.

19:02.392 --> 19:03.685
Good evening. Good evening.

19:03.769 --> 19:04.978
What's his deal?

19:06.355 --> 19:07.731
I don't know. I…

19:10.359 --> 19:12.903
I used to think that
he was scared of everything.

19:12.986 --> 19:15.072
But now I just think he's a liar.

19:19.910 --> 19:20.994
Wanna find out?

19:25.666 --> 19:27.167
Is his room upstairs?

19:29.503 --> 19:31.171
Kelly… Okay.

19:32.256 --> 19:35.968
Leave Whitewood tonight. I beg of you.

19:36.051 --> 19:40.180
- What power?
- Leave before it is too late.

19:41.640 --> 19:44.601
Kelly, I don't… I don't…
I don't think that we should go in there.

19:46.478 --> 19:48.981
If he's really lying to you,
he can't punish you.

19:49.565 --> 19:51.775
It's called the moral high ground.

20:17.301 --> 20:19.469
You're not taking me in?

20:20.387 --> 20:21.763
No.

20:21.847 --> 20:24.183
'Cause I can't listen to this all night.

20:26.143 --> 20:28.687
But I'm at my wits end, Patricia.

20:29.313 --> 20:31.398
Getting all kind of weird calls now.

20:31.899 --> 20:33.650
Fucking pulling people out the ocean.

20:33.734 --> 20:35.819
I need to know what the hell is going on.

20:36.320 --> 20:37.571
I don't know what you mean.

20:38.113 --> 20:41.366
I think you know exactly what I mean.

20:41.867 --> 20:45.162
And I know you loyal to Loftis,
but people are talking,

20:46.288 --> 20:49.291
forming some kind of
action committee or some shit,

20:49.374 --> 20:50.792
and hey, I can't blame 'em.

20:51.293 --> 20:54.171
Nobody's been able to reach the guy
for the last 24 hours.

20:54.254 --> 20:56.089
They just don't understand
what he's doing.

20:56.173 --> 20:58.258
Well, make me understand what he's doing.

20:59.176 --> 21:00.177
Huh?

21:01.345 --> 21:05.390
Because if I don't,
it's dangerous for myself, my wife,

21:05.474 --> 21:07.267
and every person on this island.

21:08.310 --> 21:10.687
I can't.
They told me not to cause a panic.

21:10.771 --> 21:15.067
Oh, Jesus Christ.
What might I panic about?

21:20.989 --> 21:22.032
Come on, Patricia.

21:24.493 --> 21:26.620
You know I've always been on your side.

21:45.597 --> 21:48.141
…approximately one mile
to the island. Low visibility.

21:55.399 --> 21:56.441
What? What is that?

21:56.525 --> 21:58.235
The island playing games.

22:03.615 --> 22:04.825
Make sure…

22:04.908 --> 22:07.578
Make sure that coffin is secure.

22:07.661 --> 22:09.121
I'm gonna check below.

22:28.265 --> 22:29.474
Who goes there?

22:32.895 --> 22:33.896
Hello.

22:34.855 --> 22:36.064
I know it's you.

22:36.940 --> 22:37.941
Please.

22:38.775 --> 22:39.902
Say something.

22:40.944 --> 22:43.697
- I feel like I'm suffocating!
- Everything's fine. Just…

22:43.780 --> 22:46.783
Just take deep breaths.

22:46.867 --> 22:51.079
Thank God. Oh, thank God. God bless you.

22:54.458 --> 22:56.126
Are you going to let me out now?

23:01.215 --> 23:04.176
Look, I can't. And I am… I'm so sorry.

23:08.096 --> 23:10.140
- It's what you promised.
- Yes, I know.

23:10.224 --> 23:14.478
I… I realize that, but I…
and I am… I am so sorry.

23:18.315 --> 23:19.483
Fuck you.

23:21.610 --> 23:23.904
- Fuck me?
- Yes. I said, "Fuck you."

23:24.655 --> 23:25.739
Fuck you!

23:25.822 --> 23:28.033
Fuck me? Fuck you!

23:28.116 --> 23:29.535
Fuck off.

23:33.539 --> 23:34.915
Are you still here?

23:36.667 --> 23:39.169
He's… He's asking to be let out.

23:41.338 --> 23:44.132
I will never understand
how the fuck you got your job.

23:46.093 --> 23:47.719
Why are you even bringing this to me?

23:48.929 --> 23:50.514
- He hasn't asked for much. He--
- Yeah.

23:50.597 --> 23:55.519
It starts as one thing and then another.
I am not letting that thing loose.

23:56.186 --> 23:58.939
Nah, you can't trust a man
that knows death's coming for him.

23:59.022 --> 24:01.275
Well, it's hard--

24:01.358 --> 24:03.902
Yeah, well of course it is!
Course it fucking is!

24:22.087 --> 24:23.088
Here.

24:26.967 --> 24:29.970
My best friend, Mark Doyle,
and his sister.

24:31.513 --> 24:32.723
My girl, Gerrie.

24:36.768 --> 24:37.936
Gerrie Doyle?

24:39.021 --> 24:40.230
That's right.

24:42.816 --> 24:44.318
Museum Gerrie?

24:44.902 --> 24:45.903
That's the one.

24:46.778 --> 24:48.947
Gerrie Doyle from the Historical Society?

24:49.031 --> 24:50.574
- I said that's the one.
- Sorry.

24:56.288 --> 24:57.664
I was just 16.

24:59.166 --> 25:01.210
It was a bad time on the island.

25:04.296 --> 25:05.797
So the island's on lockdown.

25:07.090 --> 25:10.469
There's curfews, people going missing.

25:12.095 --> 25:15.516
The perfect time for a fishing expedition.

25:17.059 --> 25:19.645
Me and my four buddies,
we decide to steal a boat,

25:19.728 --> 25:22.439
get it out on the white waves,
test our mettle.

25:22.523 --> 25:23.732
Yeah. Yeah.

25:26.276 --> 25:29.488
It struck from below at first.
Struck hard.

25:30.155 --> 25:31.823
This thing was big.

25:32.407 --> 25:34.618
It was gonna tear the boat apart
in seconds.

25:35.327 --> 25:36.995
And then I hear Ricky say he saw…

25:38.455 --> 25:39.706
saw a tentacle.

25:41.500 --> 25:45.754
Just like that, we become little boys
again screaming for our mothers,

25:45.838 --> 25:46.839
and I…

25:46.922 --> 25:50.551
…and I'm… I know I gotta get outta there.

25:51.677 --> 25:55.430
You know, before the whole thing sinks.
Before we're dragged into its mouth.

25:56.139 --> 25:58.475
And, so, I start to swim off.

25:59.935 --> 26:03.480
And that…
that's when I felt it grab my foot.

26:06.066 --> 26:07.484
I was so scared.

26:07.568 --> 26:10.737
I mean, it's… it's pulling on me,
and I'm trying to get away.

26:12.614 --> 26:17.786
And then I realize it's Mark,
begging for help.

26:19.204 --> 26:20.205
And now,

26:21.707 --> 26:23.750
we're both getting pulled under and I…

26:24.418 --> 26:26.670
and I see that thing below him.

26:27.629 --> 26:30.591
We're both getting dragged down,
and I… and I…

26:36.013 --> 26:37.264
I kicked him off me.

26:39.600 --> 26:40.684
Kicked him off me.

26:43.979 --> 26:45.606
Wyck, that wasn't your fault.

26:47.107 --> 26:50.903
I only told you that story so that
you'll listen to me one fucking time.

26:50.986 --> 26:53.405
Do not let him out!

26:56.200 --> 26:58.785
I already let him out.

27:08.462 --> 27:10.214
He can barely stand.

27:11.590 --> 27:13.133
Goddamn you to hell.

27:13.759 --> 27:15.594
Yeah. Yeah.

27:31.735 --> 27:32.778
Yeah.

27:37.491 --> 27:39.493
They only lock it if there's a secret.

28:07.521 --> 28:09.147
Is that your mom?

28:10.732 --> 28:12.234
She was so pretty.

28:21.118 --> 28:23.412
I thought you said
she died during childbirth.

28:27.332 --> 28:28.333
She did.

28:41.638 --> 28:42.764
I knew her.

28:44.725 --> 28:46.393
Well, this is sadder
than I thought it'd be.

28:46.476 --> 28:48.312
I thought it'd be like a fun secret.

28:49.479 --> 28:53.066
Yes, so my theory is
that the island corrupts.

28:53.150 --> 28:54.902
And maybe that's
what would've happened to me.

28:54.985 --> 28:58.780
I would have just been
another horrible incident in our history.

28:59.489 --> 29:00.741
Who can say?

29:01.909 --> 29:04.411
Okay, yeah, I know what that sounds like,
I… I get it.

29:04.494 --> 29:07.915
Patricia's crazy. That's… That's fine.

29:16.381 --> 29:18.800
Yeah. I'm out.

29:20.344 --> 29:21.470
Do you believe me?

29:21.553 --> 29:23.055
I just don't care to find out.

29:24.181 --> 29:27.059
Didn't like it here before
and don't like it much more now.

29:27.142 --> 29:29.186
Well, I really have only told you
the half of it--

29:29.269 --> 29:30.562
And guess what?

29:30.646 --> 29:31.730
I'm good.

29:32.981 --> 29:35.817
See. I'm good.

29:35.901 --> 29:37.986
I don't need nothing.
I don't need the other half.

29:38.070 --> 29:39.071
Do me a favor.

29:39.655 --> 29:43.116
Why don't you give my friend, the mayor,
my week's notice.

29:43.200 --> 29:44.201
That's it.

29:44.701 --> 29:45.702
- Huh?
- Okay.

29:45.786 --> 29:48.789
And feel free to help yourself out.

29:49.706 --> 29:51.917
- Okay.
- The damn thing's broken anyway.

29:53.836 --> 29:55.462
It might be fine tomorrow.

29:56.171 --> 29:57.464
Yeah, well…

29:58.465 --> 29:59.716
That sounds promising.

30:01.009 --> 30:02.636
And good luck to you all.

30:05.514 --> 30:06.723
Thank you.

30:37.796 --> 30:39.715
Oh, come, lads

30:39.798 --> 30:44.344
Let's earn our wage today

30:44.928 --> 30:48.140
Who will be the last man?

30:48.223 --> 30:49.808
You know that one, Wyck?

30:49.892 --> 30:50.976
Uh-huh.

30:51.059 --> 30:57.441
We'll board our ship and sail today

30:57.983 --> 31:02.362
Who will be the last man?

31:23.550 --> 31:24.843
We're getting close.

31:26.220 --> 31:27.888
Get the dinghy ready.

31:30.557 --> 31:32.809
I wonder what my last words will be.

31:35.312 --> 31:36.939
Will I think of my children?

31:39.525 --> 31:43.403
Something trivial? Some petty grievance?

31:46.490 --> 31:47.908
Will I think of my mother?

31:52.454 --> 31:54.456
Or will I say, "Please, God,

31:56.166 --> 31:57.251
let me live"?

32:05.259 --> 32:08.345
You know, if I made it to 60,
I'd be more than happy.

32:44.339 --> 32:46.175
No, no, no, no, no…

33:18.081 --> 33:19.291
Let's keep going.

33:31.970 --> 33:34.890
The skipper calls

33:36.225 --> 33:40.020
For a starboard tack

33:41.522 --> 33:46.610
But who will be the last one?

33:48.487 --> 33:52.199
The eastern wind

33:52.282 --> 33:54.701
Can't hold us back

33:55.827 --> 33:58.539
Though the fish are few

33:59.456 --> 34:02.334
And the water black

34:03.126 --> 34:05.128
We're gonna need a different plan.

34:10.467 --> 34:12.844
You son of a bitch! Give me that!

34:12.928 --> 34:14.888
- I wanna live!
- Give me that!

34:14.972 --> 34:18.809
Let go of me, you giant bear!
Let me go, you fucker!

34:18.891 --> 34:21.061
I'm gonna make you eat my dick!

34:24.815 --> 34:26.233
Goddamn it!

34:28.235 --> 34:30.987
Get the harpoon! Now!

34:36.368 --> 34:39.746
I don't wanna die! I don't wanna die!

35:45.437 --> 35:49.274
- Get him in the coffin!
- No! No, no, no!

35:49.358 --> 35:51.193
- Stay there.
- There!

35:56.657 --> 35:58.033
Let me live!

35:59.576 --> 36:00.577
Let me live!

36:01.828 --> 36:04.456
Let me live!

36:04.540 --> 36:06.083
Lay down!

36:21.557 --> 36:23.183
I don't wanna die!

36:31.066 --> 36:32.150
Thank y--

36:40.742 --> 36:43.579
Let me live!

37:05.809 --> 37:07.269
Shit. Shit.

37:10.105 --> 37:11.148
Shit.

37:24.661 --> 37:25.954
Damn it.

37:44.640 --> 37:45.724
Wyck!

37:48.435 --> 37:49.645
Wyck!

37:52.022 --> 37:53.524
Wyck!

38:31.228 --> 38:32.980
- I thought you were dead!
- Yeah?

38:33.063 --> 38:35.899
- Then what are you doing down there?
- I was… I was looking for flares.

38:35.983 --> 38:38.694
Yeah, so they can find you? Damn it all.

38:39.403 --> 38:41.029
This shit…

38:43.282 --> 38:45.158
Why did you move that?

39:06.763 --> 39:07.890
You did good.

39:11.185 --> 39:12.186
Thank you.

39:15.063 --> 39:16.857
I did very fucking good.

39:24.364 --> 39:26.074
Wait, did you check the coffin?

39:26.158 --> 39:27.159
Yeah.

39:27.826 --> 39:29.786
Just a lot of ribs and Vienna sausage.

39:32.956 --> 39:34.249
At least he's done singing.

40:14.289 --> 40:17.042
Yeah, perfect.
You kicked my suitcase down the stairs,

40:17.125 --> 40:20.045
- you clubfooted moron.
- It just fell. Excuse me, it fell.

40:20.128 --> 40:23.006
You have castoring rollers on the bottom,
which are a menace.

40:23.090 --> 40:24.925
This is the worst inn I've ever stayed in.

40:25.008 --> 40:28.762
- Good. Then you can leave.
- You smell like cabbage took a shit…

40:28.846 --> 40:30.430
- That's…
- …in a baby's diaper.

40:44.111 --> 40:47.990
Come lads let's earn our wage today

40:48.073 --> 40:51.159
Who will be the last man?

40:51.243 --> 40:55.289
We board the ship and sail today

40:55.372 --> 40:58.292
Who will be the last man?

40:58.375 --> 41:01.795
The eastern wind can't hold us back

41:01.879 --> 41:06.300
Though the fish are few
And the water is black

41:06.383 --> 41:09.887
The skipper calls for a starboard tack

41:09.970 --> 41:13.390
But who will be the last man?

41:13.473 --> 41:17.436
We drink our share of rum and ale

41:17.519 --> 41:20.522
Cup shot to the last man

41:20.606 --> 41:24.568
In a mighty storm of rain and hail

41:24.651 --> 41:27.696
Fighting to the last man

41:27.779 --> 41:31.617
We're drunk as sows
When the sun goes down

41:31.700 --> 41:35.662
Far and away from our island town

41:35.746 --> 41:39.291
The skipper walks the plank and drowns

41:39.374 --> 41:42.836
But who will be the last man?

41:42.920 --> 41:46.798
Ten days adrift at sea today

41:46.882 --> 41:49.927
Who will be the last man?

41:50.010 --> 41:53.597
The widows weep at home and pray

41:53.680 --> 41:57.059
That theirs will be the last man

41:57.142 --> 42:00.687
A hunger creeps for men asleep

42:00.771 --> 42:05.108
And when they wake I bare my teeth

42:05.192 --> 42:08.445
The blood and bile o'er deck they seep

42:08.529 --> 42:12.241
For I become the last man
